            "review_title": "Review at Pho Dinh Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Wingc633\nHong Kong, China2070 contributions\n0\nDelicious food\nFeb 2019 • Friends\nIt is located next to Saigon Square so it is easily be accessible by walk or car if you are in the city center. I went there for lunch on 23 February 2019.\nWe ordered 2 lunch sets, 1 beef chop, 1 chicken fillet and 1 assorted vegetables. \nThe beef chop and the chicken fillet were delicious.\nThe environment there was average, to me it was a bit noisy on the day I visited. The service there was so so, the waiters and waitress were not as efficient as what I had expected but the price was reasonable. The total of my bill was around 35 dollars.\nJust to the conclusion, I would like to recommend it to those who likes BBQ food. It is because of its location, price and food.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 7, 2019",
