            "review_text": "A Teenagers Travels\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam9 contributions\n1\nDelicious food, comfy, cheap and cute !!🍜💓\nJan 2019 • Family\nSo my mum and I were just wandering around the streets after shopping for a bit and I was stupidly hungry🙄. Literally I just pointed to the first restaurant I saw and we went in. Pho Dinh Japanese Restsurant was a pretty good random pick if I say so myself. We were immediately greeted with friendly smiles and were assisted upstairs where we were seated in a little booth. It was so cute !! 💓 This was the cheapest most comfortable and yummy lunch we I have come across so far in Ho Chi Minh. Around $14.00 AU for both mum and I and I was actually full after. I had a spicy ramen and oh my goshhhhhh it was good. This restaurant was cute, a great atmosphere and the food was pretty damn good. 🤩🍜\nRead more\nWritten January 5, 2019",
