            "review_title": "Review at Pho Dinh Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Mervyn33\nSingapore, Singapore353 contributions\n0\nJapanese - Korean BBQ\nJun 2018 • Friends\nJapanese - Korean BBQ in the heart of district 1 in HCMC, conveniently located a few metres from Saigon Square.\n\nI been there a year back .. no change to the restaurant except orders for food at the second floor is done by key into the tablet whatever you want.\nHowever the not so good part is .. the menu doesn't indicate the contents .. for example if I want to order the set for 3 or 4 people .. it doesn't tell me what is in the set. \nPreviously the hard copy menu do tell you the content and pictures of the contents.\n\nOverall the foods is still good ... we had some beef (short rib, outside skirt and tongue) and pork which were well marinated and the Uraetei dipping sauce enhances the meat flavour.\n\nYou can create your own dipping sauces ... I mix them with garlic, paprika, green spring onion and fresh chilli to give some ' kick ' \nYou can either just have the meats or wrap them with lettuce ... 2 method .. dip the meats with the sauce then wrap it with the lettuce or wrap the meats with lettuce then dip the sauce.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 19, 2018",
