            "review_title": "Review at Pho Dinh Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "493Ron\nJacksonville, Florida860 contributions\n0\nJapanese? This Seems to Me Like Korean BBQ\nJan 2018 • Family\nThis restaurant is very similar to many restaurants in Korea where the table has a grill in the center. One orders sets of desired meats: Beef, pork, seafood, vegetables, etc and then the diners grill the food themselves and eat with different sauces and garnishes. One can also order assorted salads and side dishes to go with the meat. Seems like Korean BBQ to me - I don't know where the Japanese comes in. Food was good. Service is odd and not very happy. The idea of the smiling waiter is completely alien.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 9, 2018",
